WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.018
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:14.018 --> 00:00:20.318
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:29.668
Ten and a Half: manage points and hand types
Watch all four hands from N. E banks first. Each bettor competes only against the banker; going over 10.5 busts the hand.

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:37.318
Aces count 1, 2–10 their face value, and J/Q/K half a point. Start with 1,000 chips; two banker rotations make four hands with two seats.

00:00:37.318 --> 00:00:46.118
Bettors stake chips; the banker does not
N chooses the 100 chip and clicks Bet. Use − / + for steps of 10. After dealing, only your own first, face-down card is visible.

00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:53.319
Bet 10–200 within your stack. Other pending amounts and hole cards remain private.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:01:06.319
Hit for a public up card
N’s hole card is a ten. Click Hit to draw. Exceeding 10.5 busts immediately; exactly 10.5 or a fifth card automatically finishes the hand.

00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:14.569
After bettors finish, the banker still acts
N has reached ten and a half and finished automatically. E chooses Stand. Only after both finish are the hole cards revealed and the hand settled.

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:21.319
There is no dealer-17 rule here. Bankers freely hit or stand, and still take a turn even when all bettors bust.

00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:33.318
Hand two: N becomes banker
The first hand has been revealed and settled. N now banks while E bets. N skips betting and waits for the bettor’s turn to finish.

00:01:33.318 --> 00:01:41.568
An opponent’s hit does not reveal the hole card
E clicks Hit. The new up card is public, but N still cannot see E’s hole card. Watch the finished marker to know when your turn begins.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:48.318
Rule card: a busted bettor always loses, even if the banker busts too. Equal hand types and points favor the banker.

00:01:48.318 --> 00:02:00.318
N’s banker turn
N now acts with a private two. Click Hit to draw. Bankers see their own hole card, not their opponent’s.

00:02:00.318 --> 00:02:10.768
Stand to reveal and settle the hand
N has 5 points. Click Stand. With both players finished, the server reveals all hole cards and updates stacks according to the result.

00:02:10.768 --> 00:02:19.318
A winner gets the stake back plus stake × its own multiplier. A loser pays stake × the banker’s multiplier, capped at its starting stack. A short banker pays proportionally.

00:02:19.318 --> 00:02:30.317
Hand three: another route is five cards
E banks again and N bets 100. Watch the card count this hand: the hole card counts, and five cards is the limit.

00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:42.967
Speed through hits while tracking points and count
Starting with the private two, N repeatedly clicks Hit. This accelerated sequence shows four public draws; the fifth card automatically ends N’s turn.

00:02:42.967 --> 00:02:53.316
Rule card: five face cards ×5 > five cards totaling 10.5 ×4 > five cards below 10.5 ×3 > ten and a half ×2 > ordinary points ×1.

00:02:53.316 --> 00:03:06.316
Special hands outrank ordinary point totals
N has five cards without busting: a Five Small hand. E now hits; wait for E to finish before showdown. E’s hole card is still private.

00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:13.466
Speed through the fourth hand and final rotation
Hand three is settled. In the final hand N banks, E bets and stands, then N hits. Continue until all four hands have settled normally.

00:03:13.466 --> 00:03:19.316
Below 10 chips a seat cannot bet but still banks. Fewer than two seats able to bet ends the match early.

00:03:19.316 --> 00:03:35.300
Four hands complete: final stacks decide the match
N finishes with 1,500 and E with 500, so N wins. The match covered ten and a half, a bust, Five Small and a banker bust: points alone do not determine every result.
